To blend different audio files and create a realistic experience of a summer day using Java, you can use the AudioSystem class provided by Java's media framework. Here is an example of how you could do it:
```java
import java.io.File;
import javax.sound.sampled.AudioInputStream;
import javax.sound.sampled.AudioSystem;
import javax.sound.sampled.Clip;
import javax.sound.sampled.LineUnavailableException;
import javax.sound.sampled.UnsupportedAudioFileException;

public class SummerDayAudio {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            // Load the natural sound clips
            File birdClip = new File("bird.wav");
            File leafRustleClip = new File("leaf_rustle.wav");
            File cicadaHumClip = new File("cicada_hum.wav");

            // Load the artificial sound clip
            File artificialSoundClip = new File("artificial_sound.mp3");

            // Create the natural sound clips as Clip objects
            Clip birdClipInstance = AudioSystem.getClip();
            birdClipInstance.open(AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(birdClip));
            Clip leafRustleClipInstance = AudioSystem.getClip();
            leafRustleClipInstance.open(AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(leafRustleClip));
            Clip cicadaHumClipInstance = AudioSystem.getClip();
            cicadaHumClipInstance.open(AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(cicadaHumClip));

            // Play each sound clip sequentially
            birdClipInstance.start();
            Thread.sleep(1000); // Wait for 1 second
            leafRustleClipInstance.start();
            Thread.sleep(2000); // Wait for 2 seconds
            cicadaHumClipInstance.start();
            Thread.sleep(3000); // Wait for 3 seconds

            // Stop all sound clips
            birdClipInstance.stop();
            leafRustleClipInstance.stop();
            cicadaHumClipInstance.stop();

            // Load the artificial sound clip
            Clip artificialSoundClipInstance = AudioSystem.getClip();
            artificialSoundClipInstance.open(AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(artificialSoundClip));

            // Play the artificial sound clip
            artificialSoundClipInstance.start();

            // Wait for 5 seconds
            Thread.sleep(5000);

            // Close all Clips
            birdClipInstance.close();
            leafRustleClipInstance.close();
            cicadaHumClipInstance.close();
            artificialSoundClipInstance.close();
        } catch (UnsupportedAudioFileException | IOException | LineUnavailableException e) {
            System.err.println(e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
```
This program will play three natural sound clips sequentially and then play one artificial sound clip. It uses the `Thread.sleep()` method to pause between each sound clip.
